<h1>Monet S. Wilson</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 29th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Independent. Declared write-in.</p>
<p>These names are not printed on the ballot. To vote for one, write the name in the blank write-in space for that office and fill in the oval (on a touchscreen, follow the write-in steps on screen). Votes count only for write-ins who filed a declaration. The Chicago Board of Elections does not post those names, so this list comes from the Cook County Clerk&#39;s list and campaign announcements; election judges at your polling place have the official one.</p>
<p><a href="https://wilsonil29.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (wilsonil29.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Declared write-in candidate; the name is not printed on the ballot. Calls herself a centrist and says she would lower property taxes through circuit-breaker relief and changes to how Illinois funds schools, revise parts of the SAFE-T Act to hold repeat violent offenders accountable, and push ethics enforcement and balanced budgets before tax increases.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Calumet City 2nd Ward alderwoman in her second term; she ran against Thaddeus Jones in the 2022 Democratic primary.</p>
